				<guid>http://localhost:1313/blog/math/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;inline-math&#34; class=&#34;mt-8 mb-3 text-xl sm:text-2xl text-white&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;relative inline-block&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      Inline Math&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute left-0 -bottom-1 h-px w-0 bg-indigo-400&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The quadratic formula is $x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}$, used to solve any quadratic equation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Euler&amp;rsquo;s identity, $e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0$, is considered one of the most beautiful equations in mathematics.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Pythagorean theorem states that $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$ for any right triangle.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;block-math&#34; class=&#34;mt-8 mb-3 text-xl sm:text-2xl text-white&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;relative inline-block&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      Block Math&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute left-0 -bottom-1 h-px w-0 bg-indigo-400&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Gaussian integral:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
